`/sso/start` now gates on the `sso` license feature before it will start an OIDC flow, falling back to the same silent redirect to `/login` as an unconfigured provider.

```16:22:apps/backend/src/routes/sso.ts
export const ssoRoutes = async (app: App) => {
	app.get('/sso/start', async (request, reply) => {
		if (!(await hasFeature(LICENSE_FEATURES.sso)) || !isOidcConfigured()) {
			return reply.redirect(LOGIN_PATH, 302);
		}
```

This matches how `authConfigRoutes.oidc.getConfig` and `authConfigRoutes.microsoft.isSetup` gate the same feature. Without it, an unlicensed instance that had OIDC env vars set would reach `startOidcAuthorization` and fail inside better-auth (the generic-oauth plugin is only registered when `hasFeature(sso)` is true in `apps/backend/src/auth.ts`), producing a logged error rather than a clean redirect. Lint passes across all three workspaces.

