content.text:
A single configured provider now renders as one full-width button reading "Continue with Okta" (or whatever the provider name is), and the email/password block shrinks whenever any provider is on screen so the provider button reads as the primary path.

Three pieces make that up:

`AuthSocialButton` gained a `showLabel` flag. Icon-only stays the default for the multi-provider grid; with the label it also grows to `h-11` and picks up medium weight text.

```146:171:apps/frontend/src/components/ui/button.tsx
function AuthSocialButton({
	icon: Icon,
	label,
	onClick,
	showLabel = false,
	className,
}: {
	// ...
}) {
	return (
		<Button
			// ...
			className={cn('h-10 w-full rounded-lg', showLabel && 'h-11 gap-2.5 text-sm font-medium', className)}
			onClick={onClick}
		>
			<Icon className='size-4 text-foreground [&_path]:fill-current' />
			{showLabel && label}
		</Button>
	);
}
```

The provider renderers in `auth-form.tsx` previously took a bare `className` string; they now take a props object so `showLabel` can be threaded alongside it, spread straight onto each button. `MicrosoftSignInButton` and `OidcSignInButton` forward the new prop. Full width came for free — a single provider already gets `grid-cols-1` and the buttons are `w-full`.

For the de-emphasis I added a small context in `auth-form.tsx`, set to true when providers are displayed, that `FormTextField` reads. The inputs go from `h-12`/`text-base` to `h-10`/`text-sm`, labels from `text-sm` to `text-xs`, and the submit button from `h-11` to `h-10`. Doing it through context rather than a prop means the routes that render fields as children don't need to know about provider configuration, and the fields keep their original size on pages with no providers (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`) plus in the settings password form, which uses `FormTextField` outside `AuthForm`. I also tightened the login page's own field margins slightly (`mb-6`→`mb-4`, `mb-10`→`mb-8`) since those live in the route.

Lint passes across all three workspaces. Per the repo's testing note I left visual verification to you — worth a look at the two-provider and three-provider cases to confirm the icon-only grid still looks right next to the compacted fields.

