The "Last used" marker is now a shared pill component used in both places.

```1:14:apps/frontend/src/components/ui/last-used-pill.tsx
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

export function LastUsedPill({ className }: { className?: string }) {
	return (
		<span
			className={cn(
				'rounded-full border bg-background px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium leading-none text-muted-foreground',
				className,
			)}
		>
			Last used
		</span>
	);
}
```

It carries no positioning of its own, so each caller places it. On a provider button it floats over the top border at `-top-2 right-3`, with the opaque background punching through the button outline. On the email option it sits inline next to the label, since a badge floating above a plain text link would look untethered.

One consequence worth flagging: the email/password form no longer auto-expands when it was your last method. It couldn't do both — an expanded form means the toggle is gone, and the pill with it. So the toggle now always shows, carrying the pill when email was last used, which costs a click but keeps the hint visible and makes all the sign-in options read the same way. Say the word if you'd rather have the auto-expand back and drop the pill there.

